                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Chinese Inn seems like it could be a fine little re-release of an old game if it worked properly.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/WOjM1hS1tPE?t=1h12m41s\n\nThis game has some major issues running properly on new hardware to the point where it is basically un-playable.\n\nThe game window is very small but manageable, this should be updated to be more than a couple inches big though.\n\nAll of the english font in the game does not line up with where you are intended to click in the game. This is not because the english words were longer or anything, they were improperly implemented so they are always covering up other parts of the UI and not in line with the game window at all.\n\nThere are multiple buttons in the game that don't work or seem to stop working.\n\nThe opening cutscene does not seem to work properly. The game runs it at about 5x speed due to what I think is because of new computers processing it too fast.\n\nIt's very sad because I see where this game could have been very fun in it's day. I love the artstyle and the idea of running an inn, I just wish it worked properly.\n\nIf you found this review helpful, follow my curator page to see everything I cover. http://store.steampowered.com/curator/29029552/",
